WEBVTT

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.810
We will capture the Dragon Torque
and return to La'cryma.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.780
Tobi, can you manage?

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.250
I'll try.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:41.330
It will create a strain at the time
of transposition, but I think I can do it.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.270
Karasu!

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:45.980
The Dragon Torque!

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:51.990
What is this?

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.360
Rapid approach of alternate dimension!

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:01.620
What is that?

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.590
What?

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:08.350
Shangri-la?

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:15.860
A floating mask.

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.230
Hear me, Dragon Torque.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:21.680
Dragon Torque.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:27.270
What is this undulation?!

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.970
The time has not arrived.

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.210
What do you mean?

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:35.190
Noein! Why are you here?!

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:36.570
Who are you?

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.900
You fools...

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.830
You're just scum in space.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:55.760
I will not permit you
to have the Dragon Torque.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:57.870
Under any circumstances.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:03.560
I will never defile
the Dragon Torque.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.320
Damn it!

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.720
Karasu, go after the Dragon Torque!

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.050
But...

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:12.650
Just go!

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:19.290
Leave, those who do not exist...

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.120
in this dimension.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:41.680
At the silver sky, the endless sky

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:48.020
I gazed together with you, without a word

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:54.190
Touching your back, with trembling fingers

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.610
I quietly ponder, as your profile looks up

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:05.660
I want to assure your smile, and the future ahead of you

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:12.000
Just standing and crying, I want to erase myself away

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:17.880
As I extend my hands, it is almost within my reach

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:23.930
This is no fantasy, possibilities are perhaps right by my side

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:29.770
Changing every sorrow into strength

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:35.940
Let's throw all limitations into the end of time

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.150
Just keeping you as my aspirations

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:44.280
Even in the driving wind

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:51.210
I'll still be pushing on ahead

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:56.880
Misekku kesta

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:04.800
Fortune. Will you save it for me, dear?

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.880
Straight, straight!
Keep going straight.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:15.980
Got it.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.540
The reading is getting stronger.
It's around here.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:22.490
First a mountain and now a warehouse?

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:25.290
Make a right there.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.620
Roger.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.700
What's this? I've never seen
this type of wavelength before.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.030
You sure it's right?

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:33.460
Just drive.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.760
You gotta be kidding!

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.130
Ow...

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.610
Huh?

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:47.840
Are you okay?!

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.770
Did you get hurt, little girl?

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:53.310
Well... I think I'm okay.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.730
Is that you, Haruka-chan?

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:56.730
Uchida-san!

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.730
Are you sure you're okay?
No cuts or bruises?

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:00.960
I'm fine.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.350
That's good. But it's dangerous
to run out in front of cars.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.740
I didn't run in front of any cars...

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:11.740
Oh, yeah...

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:24.760
There's nobody in here.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.550
But that can't be.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.450
Haruka-chan, you shouldn't
play pranks on adults.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:30.550
But they were really here!

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:34.420
Oh, come on. Don't tell me
you hit your head back there.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:38.450
Hey! What's wrong, kid?!

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.970
What is it?

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:56.640
I'm sorry! I have to be going now.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.740
Haruka-chan?!

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:02.210
I wonder what got into her?

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.240
You can't tell what's going on
in the heads of kids nowadays.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:24.360
Uchida-chan, have you heard
of any insects that eat bricks?

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:26.940
Are you trying to test
my trivial knowledge?

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:28.740
Damn, I hate middle-aged men.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.740
Maybe we should check
this place out a bit more.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:35.950
There are tiny holes in this brick wall.

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:39.790
Kind of like it was
burned through with lasers.

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:44.950
It's got be someone with way
too much time on their hands.

00:06:57.710 --> 00:07:01.280
<i>Irregularity. Five birds have returned.</i>

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.110
<i>Signs of life have been detected.</i>

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:06.140
<i>Send in the medical team immediately.</i>

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:11.820
Karasu...

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:26.820
It wasn't about Yuu after all.

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.700
Maybe it's me they want.

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:46.790
Yuu! It's time to go to cram school.

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:48.940
Yuu!

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.530
Fujiwara?

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:02.200
Hello?

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:05.580
Hey, it's me! Kaminogi,
are you doing anything?

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:14.120
Hey!

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:15.720
What is it, Fujiwara?

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.620
Well, I stopped by Yuu's house, and...

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:21.220
Yuu's house? How did it go?

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:24.730
Didn't get anywhere.
His mom won't let me see him.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:26.150
I knew it.

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:29.400
It looks like she
took his cell phone too.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.830
Isn't there a better plan?

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:33.610
Let me think...

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:38.110
Clara, don't eat stuff off the street.

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:40.000
And don't eat frogs either.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.030
Huh? Haruka...

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:50.880
C... Could this be?

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.990
There's nothing particularly
special about that.

00:08:55.990 --> 00:09:00.430
I wonder! They were talking together
looking really serious...

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.700
when suddenly they looked into
each other's eyes and smiled!

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:05.100
Th... They did?

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.360
Oh, what a shocker!

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.440
Why is it a shocker?

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:13.470
I used Agnes Yamada's love horoscope...

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:16.540
to check out my compatibility
with the boys in the class.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:20.740
And it said, Fujiwara-kun and I were a match!

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.240
Uh-huh?

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:26.720
Next, I checked Haruka
and Fujiwara-kun's compatibility.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:28.020
Haruka and Fujiwara?

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:30.560
You know what it said? Surprise, surprise!

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:32.630
They're a perfect match!

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:33.730
W-Wow...

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:37.270
I'm sure Haruka's
read that horoscope too!

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:42.340
Besides, Fujiwara-kun always acts a little weird when he talks to her.

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.900
He's obviously totally nuts for her!

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:53.810
Destroy the Dragon Torque?

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:59.710
We can't, Atori. Our mission is
to secure it, not to destroy it.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:02.150
That thing is dangerous.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:08.720
I can tell. She's the cause
of this screwed-up dimension.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:13.830
That's why we have to destroy her.
If we don't, this entire universe...

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:16.470
...will be obliterated.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:24.570
This La'cryma is finished... and so is the Dragon Torque.

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:28.880
So what now? Do you want to come with me?

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:31.920
Or...

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:44.200
What's wrong, Ai?
Hey, you're here too, Miho.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:48.240
Isami was just at your house, wasn't he?

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:50.710
Oh, Fujiwara?
How'd you know that?

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:53.210
So, what was he doing there?

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:56.040
Why does that matter?

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:59.720
D-Don't blow it off.
Answer the question, Haruka!

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:00.820
But...

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:02.950
What are you waiting for?!

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:07.660
Existence and nothingness...

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:11.330
are in the place
indicated by the Uroboros.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:12.860
Who said that?

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:17.260
Hear me, Dragon Torque.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:25.410
Surely those who exist in
this universe will seek you out.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:26.870
Haruka?

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.280
Are you listening to me?

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:32.080
- There's a strange man over there.
- Huh?

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:35.590
Where? Where is he, Haruka?

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:37.150
He disappeared.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:39.090
Hey, Haruka!

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.190
Really, Haruka!

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:45.350
It's him.

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:47.390
Him?

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:50.690
He was here.

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.670
Someone's after you? Who?

00:11:56.670 --> 00:12:00.400
Wasn't it Goto they were after?

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:03.820
It looks like me after all.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:06.150
You?

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:07.740
I'm tired of your made-up stories!

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:09.330
I'm not lying.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:13.150
Anyway, answer my question
as to why Goto went to your house!

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:15.710
Like I said, he was worried about Yuu.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:19.120
When he goes to Yuu's house,
Yuu's mom just turns him away.

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:22.380
Of course, she won't
let me see him either.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:28.200
He'll go crazy if he's locked himself
in the house like that. So...

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:30.540
Fujiwara came over because
he was worried about Yuu...

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:31.890
Oh, forget it!

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:33.710
Let's go, Miho!

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:36.400
Huh? We're going? Ai?!

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:41.010
What's with her? Why is she so angry?

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:53.540
You can't do it.

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:59.460
Haruka will eventually
disappear from your sight.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.400
What are you doing here?

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.500
I see the fear in your eyes.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:15.770
You can't possibly protect Haruka.
It's impossible.

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:18.270
Because you're me.

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:20.350
Wh... Who the hell are you?!

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:45.810
It can't go on like this.

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:57.190
If I'm with you, his mom
will be even more upset.

00:13:58.030 --> 00:14:00.030
So persuading her
together won't work, huh?

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:02.000
How about we get advice
from Yukie-chan?

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:05.870
No way!
That'd make his mom even madder.

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:07.610
That won't be fair to Yuu.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:09.280
That's true.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:13.490
She used to be really nice too.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:15.340
Yeah.

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:18.640
Our hands are tied for now.

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:22.710
Have you come up with something?

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:26.350
Oops, I almost forgot. Here.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.510
The same cell strap as Ai has.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:31.290
It's the baby chicken of fortune.

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:34.290
Fumiko made another one,
so I'll let you have one too.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:39.190
Wow, it's cute! Thanks!

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:51.170
I got mail.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:53.110
Huh?

00:14:53.110 --> 00:14:54.160
What is it?

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:56.650
Sorry, I have to go!

00:14:56.650 --> 00:14:58.160
What?! Kaminogi!

00:14:59.090 --> 00:15:00.720
I'll call you again!

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:05.170
Geez.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:13.390
Ai!

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:20.470
I also wanted to tell you
something.

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:23.880
Listen, about yesterday...

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:25.230
Why?

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:28.240
What was Fujiwara doing at
your house again today?

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:30.420
Like I said, we were talking about Yuu.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:32.240
I heard that story yesterday.

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:36.520
We were having another talk
about going to Yuu's house together.

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:38.860
Yuu, Yuu, Yuu!

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:41.040
So you're gonna blame it all on Goto.

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:42.950
Hey! What's with your attitude!

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:46.260
All right, ask Fujiwara yourself.
I'll call him right now.

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:49.830
Where did you get that?!

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:53.680
Oh, this? Fujiwara gave
one to you too, right?

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:03.770
You're always like that!
You only care about yourself!

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:07.910
What did I do to deserve that?!

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:09.660
Ow...

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:13.390
You know damn well!
Don't act like a natural born idiot!

00:16:13.390 --> 00:16:14.960
Who are you calling
a natural born idiot?!

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:18.130
You goody-goody!

00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:20.560
You're not making sense!

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:22.740
Don't play dumb!

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:24.200
I'm not!

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.300
You are, Haruka!

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:28.240
Why would I?!

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:31.010
- Stupid!
- Moron!

00:16:44.590 --> 00:16:46.160
I've had it!

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:50.660
I hate you, Haruka!

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.320
And I hate Fujiwara too.

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:57.070
What do you mean?! Ai, you idiot!

00:16:57.810 --> 00:16:59.490
Geez.

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.880
Wow, what a cute thing you got there.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:11.050
My little sister Fumiko made it.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:15.010
Gee, do you even need
a good-luck charm?

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:18.790
You'd just lose it
if you kept it, Fujiwara.

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:22.350
This cell strap is happier
being owned by me!

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:24.830
Don't you lose it either.

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:26.290
Bleagh!

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:34.670
I'm a real bitch.

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:50.920
I haven't had a fight
like that in a long time.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.260
That hurts...

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:00.570
Haruka? I'll leave a change
of clothes for you here.

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:02.000
Thanks!

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:05.770
And brush your teeth
before going to sleep.

00:18:06.110 --> 00:18:07.570
I will.

00:18:08.010 --> 00:18:11.650
And if you've had a fight,
you should patch things up ASAP.

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:14.860
How...

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.020
How could you tell?

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:19.390
In your case, it's
written all over your face.

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:21.660
What?! How come?

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.550
You should apologize first, Haruka.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:28.390
Even if you think you're right,
you apologize first.

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:30.960
That's the trick to
patching up a friendship.

00:18:32.470 --> 00:18:37.300
It'd be real lonely to lose
a good friend over something silly.

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:41.300
Baron, what should I do?

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.780
Mom says I should apologize.

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:50.280
But what did I do...

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:52.480
to get Ai mad at me?

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:56.690
I just don't get it.

00:18:58.070 --> 00:18:59.200
Huh?

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:04.790
It's raining.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.140
Where am I?

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:28.140
This is one of your near futures.

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:31.350
It's gone. It's gone...

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:33.630
I lost it.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:35.400
This is the future?

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:42.410
I've lost both the cell strap
and a friend.

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:44.620
Cell strap?

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:53.850
Cell strap...

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:05.880
I've had it!

00:20:06.590 --> 00:20:08.760
I hate you, Haruka!

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:12.470
Hasebe, want some?

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:15.240
You know you can't bring
junk food to school.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:18.000
Oh! I bet you do want some.

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:20.340
Ow, ow, ow! Forgive me!

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:21.710
- No forgiveness!
- Stop it!

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:24.340
- Haruka, grab the chocolate! Hurry, hurry!
- Hey, come on!

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:26.830
Ai, bullying is bad.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:29.330
Ow! You'll break it, you'll break it!

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:30.820
I won't stop.

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:32.710
No way!

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:39.520
Ai likes Fujiwara...

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:49.100
I'm going out for a minute!

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:52.830
What? Where are you going in this rain?!
Haruka? Haruka?!

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.430
Ai...

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.680
It's the same as before.

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:33.140
Where? Where did it go?

00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:35.080
It's gone...

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.200
What are you doing?

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.060
Just looking for something.

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:50.390
Nobody asked you!

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:52.360
I know.

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:57.200
Do what you want.

00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:58.800
Okay, I will.

00:22:26.970 --> 00:22:29.070
I found it! I found it, Ai!

00:22:29.070 --> 00:22:30.530
Really?!

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:33.170
See?

00:22:34.440 --> 00:22:35.910
You found it!

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:38.410
That's a relief.

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:40.080
Yeah!

00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:43.780
I'm sorry, Ai.

00:22:44.120 --> 00:22:46.910
No, I'm the one who should apologize.

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:50.550
I'm sorry, Haruka. Will you forgive me?

00:22:51.190 --> 00:22:54.620
We're best friends, now and forever.

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:30.380
A sleepless night

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:34.270
The sound of the second hand

00:23:34.270 --> 00:23:41.200
The rumble of the
refrigerator in the air

00:23:42.100 --> 00:23:45.990
Just as the moon
through the blinds...

00:23:45.990 --> 00:23:49.900
Waxes and wanes, someday...

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:56.490
The pain will change to warmth

00:23:56.490 --> 00:24:01.710
Boat of time...

00:24:02.300 --> 00:24:06.960
No matter where it flows...

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:13.090
Most likely we'll meet again

00:24:13.090 --> 00:24:16.730
From scars come the
footsteps of dawn

00:24:16.730 --> 00:24:19.930
Rather than sighing,
they secretly...

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:26.040
come pouring down
on every new day

00:24:26.040 --> 00:24:30.580
No matter what sky it is

00:24:41.970 --> 00:24:43.930
I'm dreaming again.

00:24:45.040 --> 00:24:46.730
That summer day's dream.

00:24:48.440 --> 00:24:50.720
You have to chant with me!

00:24:53.950 --> 00:24:55.820
Atori and the others.

00:24:55.820 --> 00:24:57.430
Be on your guard.

00:25:00.420 --> 00:25:03.480
It's all an illusion, Dragon Torque.

00:25:04.360 --> 00:25:06.750
Next, And Then...

00:25:07.860 --> 00:25:10.000
What'll happen to me?
